          "heading": "Jake White's Fiji slump to fourth straight defeat, 54-17 to France",
          "body": "Fiji coach Jake White's side started with 10 France-based players, including their entire backline, and were typically physical. Their much-vaunted backs struggled to fire. Simione Kuruvoli's penalty was their only reward before the break, when France led 26-3. Selestino Ravutaumada added a second consolation try, while Jiuta Wainiqolo, playing in his adopted home, was unable to make an impact."
