          "kicker": "Pollock hype",
          "heading": "Victor Matfield questions Henry Pollock's hype after his two tries against Australia",
          "body": "Former Springboks second row Victor Matfield has questioned the fuss around Henry Pollock on the Rugby Rivals podcast. He cannot see why so much is expected of him. Matfield argued the credit for Pollock's second try, a run to the corner unopposed, belongs to the team-mates who got him the ball. Former All Blacks and Italy coach John Kirwan disagreed, saying England need a superstar and that Pollock is one. Pollock came on at half-time against Australia, moved to the wing and scored twice in two minutes."
