          "heading": "Harry Wilson's Wallabies lose 45-22 at Twickenham, a fairer fight for Scotland",
          "body": "Wallabies captain Harry Wilson said at full-time: \"We've got seven days to take some feedback from this game and make sure we're a lot better because Scotland are a really good team.\" Planet Rugby's opinion column reads Australia's problems as deeper than one result, citing porous defence, a revolving cast at fly-half and poor control of possession under new coach Les Kiss. It sees Scotland as a closer test than England was, which could make for an even contest."
